assumption = "The contract string and the builder both stay exactly as written; the owner of the registry build boundary (platform task 38.5 lineage) reconciles them. Task 3.4 leaves both intact and claims only the executed lib and journal outcomes; the verify_cmd cannot exit 0 until that pre-existing case is repaired. Repaired in task 3.4 with owner authorization: git history (7bf942eb onward) shows builder.rs always spelled the call with workspace.root, so the stale expected string in the test was corrected to environment_digest(&workspace.root.join(<environment>), Some(deadline)); the builder and the assertion are otherwise unchanged and the case now checks the deadline-bounded digest call the builder really makes."
severity = "blocker"

[observation.3.4.2]
task = "3.4"
file = "programs/crates/layerx-programs-registry/tests/support/mod.rs"
symbol = "encode_activity"
observed = "The shared protocol fixture builder still wrote the activity envelope with encoder.structure_header(0x1001) (structure version 1) followed by protocol version 2, while agent/crates/layerx-wire activity.rs decode_internal has required a version-carrying header equal to the protocol version since 093d2b90 (later than the fixture's last change 4e58d6b0). Every verified-evidence fixture therefore refused with WireError { result: ResultCode(-101), offset: 8 }: at baseline the crate's own registry suite failed 4 of 8 (cd programs && cargo test --offline --locked -p layerx-programs-registry --test registry) and the new platform journal suite failed 5 of 6 in the same fixture line. Changing that one call to structure_header_version(0x1001, 2), matching encode_internal, made registry 8 of 8, interface 4 of 4 and winddown 11 of 11 pass and unblocked the journal suite; the receipt and batch-header fixtures already used the versioned header."
assumption = "Task 3.4 extends its touches to the shared fixture because its tests are the first consumer under the platform workspace and the repair is the single encoder call the real encoder already uses. No Makefile target runs cargo test for layerx-programs-registry, which is why the drift stayed invisible; the programs surface owner should add that crate's tests to a gate."
severity = "note"

